  "quotes": [
    {
      "block": "原句1",
      "no": 1,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "The only thing better than a good joke is a really, really bad joke",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 43
        }
      ],
      "words": 14
    },
    {
      "block": "原句2",
      "no": 2,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "There has been endless research done into the positive effects of humour in social connections, improving one’s mood and",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 150
        },
        {
          "text": "It unites us as humans. You can’t hate someone who is making you laugh",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 396
        }
      ],
      "words": 41
    },
    {
      "block": "原句3",
      "no": 3,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "So a good joke is useful. Think of it like a canoe: a functional item that does a job and gets you from A to B",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 467
        }
      ],
      "words": 26
    },
    {
      "block": "原句4",
      "no": 4,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "There are 700-ish jokes in this book, and a lot of them aren’t any good at all. Some are corny and predictable, some are",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 579
        }
      ],
      "words": 32
    },
    {
      "block": "原句5",
      "no": 5,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "But a bad joke brings a whole extra level to the experience. The right kind of bad joke is slightly funny on its own mer",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 753
        }
      ],
      "words": 33
    },
    {
      "block": "原句6",
      "no": 6,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "So it’s bad, absolutely, but it’s also better. Or, to put it another way, you can have your kayak and heat it too",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 1577
        }
      ],
      "words": 23
    }
  ],
